d></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-6163158-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>6163158</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-62013357-Y2" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>62013357</doc-number><kind>Y2</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8288069-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8288069</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TDK CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TDK CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ARAI MICHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARAI, MICHIO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A thin light-emitting diode which a large-area display is relatively easily constructed of, has a long life, is produced at low cost, and is adaptable to full-color display, comprising an anode, a cathode, an inorganic light-emitting layer provided between the electrodes and causing at least electroluminescence, an inorganic electron transport layer provided between the inorganic light-emitting layer and the cathode and containing as a main component one or more oxides selected from the group consisting of strontium oxide, magnesium oxide, calcium oxide, lithium oxide, rubidium oxide, potassium oxide, sodium oxide, and cesium oxide, and an inorganic insulating hole transport layer provided between the inorganic light-emitting layer and the anode and containing as a main component an oxide of silicon and/or germanium.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une diode électroluminescente mince destinée à un affichage grande surface, relativement facile à fabriquer, bon marché, qui présente une longue durée de vie et s'adapte à un visuel quadrichrome. Cette diode comprend une anode, une cathode, une couche inorganique électroluminescente disposée entre les électrodes et provoquant au moins une électroluminescence, une couche inorganique de transport d'électrons disposée entre la couche inorganique électroluminescente et la cathode et contenant, comme élément principal, un ou plusieurs oxydes sélectionnés dans le groupe constitué par un oxyde de strontium, un oxyde de magnésium, un oxyde de calcium, un oxyde de de lithium, un oxyde de rubidium, un oxyde de potassium, un oxyde de sodium et un oxyde de césium. La diode comprend en outre une couche inorganique isolante de transport de trous disposée entre la couche inorganique électroluminescente et l'anode et contenant, comme élément principal, un oxyde de silicium et/ou de germanium.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>